/-!
# The sharp map, functoriality, quotients, and `p`-recovery of untilts

This file develops the morphisms attached to the untilt `untilt p P J` of a Huber pair
`P = (R, R⁺)` along an ideal `J ⊆ 𝕎 R⁺`:

* **The sharp map** `untilt.sharp p P J : R →*₀ untilt p P J` is the unique multiplicative map
  extending `x ↦ algebraMap (mk J [x])` on `R⁺` (`untilt.sharp_apply`). It carries every
  pseudouniformiser of `R` to a pseudouniformiser of the untilt
  (`untilt.isPseudoUniformizer_sharp`). When `R` is a perfect Tate ring of characteristic `p` and
  `p` is topologically nilpotent in the untilt — in particular when `J = (ξ)` is generated by a
  primitive element — `sharp` is continuous (`untilt.continuous_sharp`,
  `untilt.continuous_sharp_of_isPrimitive`).
* **Functoriality** `untilt.map` sends a ring homomorphism `f : R →+* S` carrying `P.plus` into
  `Q.plus` with `J ≤ J'.comap (WittVector.map f⁺)` to a ring homomorphism
  `untilt p P J →+* untilt p Q J'` compatible with `algebraMap` (`untilt.map_algebraMap`) and
  `sharp` (`untilt.map_sharp`), and preserving `untiltPlus` (`untilt.map_mem_untiltPlus`). No
  primitivity assumption on `J` or `J'` is needed; when `R` and `S` are Tate rings and `f` is
  continuous, `untilt.map` is continuous (`untilt.continuous_map`).
* **Quotients along a primitive element** `ξ`: `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` identifies with `untiltPlus p P (ξ)`
  (`untilt.quotientEquivPlus`), and for every `ϖ ∈ R⁺` dividing `ξ₀`,
  `untiltPlus ⧸ (sharp ϖ) ≃+* R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ)` (`untilt.quotEquiv`).
* **Recovery along `(p)`**: for a perfect Tate ring `R` of characteristic `p`,
  `untilt.pRecovery` is a ring isomorphism `untilt p P (span {p}) ≃+* R` whose inverse is `sharp`,
  which identifies `untiltPlus` with `R⁺` and is a homeomorphism whenever `R` is uniform
  (`untilt.isHomeomorph_pRecovery`).

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp`: the multiplicative sharp map `R →*₀ untilt p P J`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.map`: functoriality `untilt p P J →+* untilt p Q J'`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotientEquivPlus`: `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ) ≃+* untiltPlus p P (ξ)`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotEquiv`: `untiltPlus ⧸ (sharp ϖ) ≃+* R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ)`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.pRecovery`: `untilt p P (span {p}) ≃+* R`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_apply`, `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isPseudoUniformizer_sharp`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.continuous_sharp`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isTopologicallyNilpotent_natCast`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.continuous_sharp_of_isPrimitive`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.map_algebraMap`, `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.map_sharp`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.map_id`, `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.map_comp`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.continuous_map`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotEquiv_mk_sharp`, `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotEquiv_symm_mk`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.pRecovery_sharp`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.mem_untiltPlus_pRecovery_iff`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isHomeomorph_pRecovery`.

## References

* P. Scholze, *Étale cohomology of diamonds*, Theorem 3.17 and its proof.
* P. Scholze and J. Weinstein, *Berkeley lectures on `p`-adic geometry*, Theorem 6.2.11.
* K. S. Kedlaya, *Sheaves, stacks, and shtukas*, Theorem 2.3.9.
-/

